+# Sandbox Hardening Runbook — gVisor / Firecracker / Container hardening
+
+Purpose
+- Step-by-step guidance and automation to move PoC sandboxing to production-grade microVMs and hardened container runtimes.
+
+Scope
+- gVisor (runsc) runtimeclass for k8s
+- Ignite / Firecracker microVM service for microVM isolation
+- Seccomp profile, PodSecurity, network policies, RBAC and image hardening
+
+Prerequisites
+- Cluster admin privileges
+- containerd configured with runsc and runtimeclass enabled OR Ignite installed
+- Image build pipeline that produces minimal distroless-based images
+
+High-level steps
+1) Build hardened images (distroless/minimal) with only required runtime libs
+   - Use ops/sandbox/build_hardened_image.sh to build + scan images
+
+2) Create Seccomp & PodSecurity
+   - Apply ops/sandbox/seccomp/profile.json as a SeccompProfile (or annotate pods)
+   - Enforce PodSecurity admission (restricted policy)
+
+3) Configure RuntimeClass (ops/sandbox/k8s/runsc-runtimeclass.yaml) — ensure containerd has runsc runtime
+
+4) Use NetworkPolicy to isolate sandbox pods (deny egress by default; allow specific egress to audit services)
+   - Example: ops/sandbox/k8s/sandbox-networkpolicy.yaml
+
+5) Use RBAC to restrict who can create pods with runtimeClassName: runsc
+
+6) Use microVMs for higher isolation for high-risk jobs
+   - Ignite / Firecracker via ops/sandbox/firecracker/ignite_runner.sh
+   - Deploy a controller or operators to launch microVMs for jobs
+
+7) Monitoring & logging
+   - Ensure audit logs for sandbox start/stop, user, invoked command are written to evidence S3
+   - Integrate kube-audit and push events to central logging
+
+8) Tests & validation
+   - Run escape vectors and capture that seccomp prevents syscalls
+   - Run internal pen-tests and red-team harness against sandboxed workloads
+
+Automation scripts
+- ops/sandbox/build_hardened_image.sh — builds minimal image and runs local scanner (Trivy example)
+- ops/sandbox/run_with_runsc.sh — helper to run images under runsc (PoC)
+- ops/sandbox/firecracker/ignite_runner.sh — microVM runner (PoC)
+
+Notes & safety
+- Do not use rootless containers without proper seccomp/cgroup setups.
+- For highly sensitive workloads, prefer microVM isolation (Firecracker) over gVisor.
+- Maintain an allowlist of container images that are allowed to run with privileged runtimeclasses.
+
